% Eye Prostheses: LCD L33737 and its Policy Article A52462 (DME MACs). A
% policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for an ocular prosthesis — custom fabricated (V2623) or stock
% (V2629) — or a scleral cover shell (V2627), for the polishing and
% resurfacing of a prosthesis (V2624) or for its enlargement (V2625) or
% reduction (V2626) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY. The benefit is not durable
% medical equipment: the Policy Article places eye prostheses under the
% Medicare Artificial Legs, Arms and Eyes benefit of Social Security Act
% §1861(s)(9), so no condition on the place of use applies. A trial scleral
% shell (L9900) is in scope but in no benefit: it is included in the
% allowance for the scleral cover shell and not separately payable.
%
% The coverage criteria:
%   1. absence or shrinkage of an eye due to birth defect, trauma or
%      surgical removal — the condition and its cause are facts of the
%      record;
%   2. polishing and resurfacing (V2624) twice per year — the count of such
%      services on the prosthesis in the twelve months ending on the date of
%      service, the claim's included, is a fact of the record — a service on
%      a prosthesis is an accessory of it (the shared template, as a shoe
%      modification is of the shoe in therapeutic_shoes.le);
%   3. one enlargement or reduction (V2625, V2626) without documentation;
%      further ones only when the medical record supports their necessity —
%      the count previously furnished is a fact of the record, and the
%      necessity of a further one is a judgment: the finding "additional
%      adjustment medically necessary";
%   4. a modification (an enlargement or reduction) within 90 days of the
%      delivery of the prosthesis is included in its allowance (the
%      Article): it is separately payable only after the 90th day.
% The ocular prosthesis codes V2623 and V2629 are named by the Facial
% Prostheses Policy Article A52463, which this program cites for them; the
% Eye Prostheses texts name only the services (V2624–V2627) and the trial
% shell.
%
% Not modelled: the replacement of a prosthesis lost or irreparably damaged
% without a new order (a relaxation of the shared order requirement, for
% which dmepos.le has no hook); repairs and follow-up visits (no code the
% texts name); the PROSE device coding (V2627 or V2531 by the condition
% treated: a coding rule); the RT/LT modifiers; the jurisdiction of claims
% for implanted components and for prostheses provided in hospital.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* has *a condition* of an eye due to *a cause*; undefined.
    the number of polishing and resurfacing services on *a device* in the twelve months ending on the date of service of *a claim* is *a number*; undefined.
    the number of enlargements and reductions of *a device* previously furnished is *a number*; undefined.
    % derived
    *an item* is an eye prosthesis.
    *a beneficiary* has a qualifying eye condition.
    *an item* is a service on a covered eye prosthesis.
    *an item* is a modification separately payable after delivery of *a device*.
    the enlargement or reduction of *a device* is justified for *a claim*.

the knowledge base eye prostheses includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base eye prostheses includes:

LCD L33737 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33737".
the text of LCD L33737 is at "sources/lcd/L33737.txt".
Policy Article A52462 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52462".
the text of Policy Article A52462 is at "sources/article/A52462.txt".
Policy Article A52463 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52463".
the text of Policy Article A52463 is at "sources/article/A52463.txt".

% What an eye prosthesis is: the custom fabricated and the stock ocular
% prosthesis (the Facial Prostheses Article), the scleral cover shell.
rule eye_prosthesis_ocular with provenance Policy Article A52463,
        confer "Code V2623 describes an ocular prosthesis, which is custom fabricated. Code V2629 is used for an ocular prosthesis that is not custom fabricated (i.e., stock prosthesis)":
an item is an eye prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2623", "V2629"].

rule eye_prosthesis_scleral with provenance Policy Article A52462,
        confer "They are included in the allowance for scleral cover shells, V2627":
an item is an eye prosthesis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "V2627".

% A service on a prosthesis that is itself covered (an accessory of it): the prosthesis is
% furnished to a beneficiary with a qualifying eye condition. A device of
% this model.
rule eye_service_on_covered:
an item is a service on a covered eye prosthesis
    if the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is an eye prosthesis
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a qualifying eye condition.

section applicability is:

eye_prostheses has no specific documentation requirements.

% The codes this policy decides: the prostheses, the services on them, and
% the trial shell; the benefit — the statutory benefit of Social Security
% Act §1861(s)(9) — is not the trial shell's.
rule eye_codes with provenance Policy Article A52462,
        confer "The right (RT) and/or left (LT) modifiers must be used with all HCPCS codes in this policy":
the policy for code a code is eye_prostheses
    if the code is in ["V2623", "V2624", "V2625", "V2626", "V2627", "V2629", "L9900"].

rule eye_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52462,
        confer "Eye prostheses are covered under the Medicare Artificial Legs, Arms and Eyes benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the benefit category of code a code is "artificial legs, arms and eyes"
    if the code is in ["V2623", "V2624", "V2625", "V2626", "V2627", "V2629"].

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The claims: a prosthesis, its polishing, its enlargement or reduction.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule eye_covered with provenance LCD L33737,
        confer "Eye prostheses are covered for a beneficiary with absence or shrinkage of an eye due to birth defect, trauma or surgical removal":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an eye prosthesis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a qualifying eye condition.

rule eye_polishing with provenance LCD L33737,
        confer "Polishing and resurfacing (V2624) is covered on a twice per year basis":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "V2624"
    and the item is a service on a covered eye prosthesis
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the number of polishing and resurfacing services on the device in the twelve months ending on the date of service of the claim is a number
    and the number <= 2.

rule eye_enlargement with provenance LCD L33737,
        confer "One enlargement (V2625) or reduction (V2626) of the prosthesis is covered without documentation":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["V2625", "V2626"]
    and the item is a service on a covered eye prosthesis
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the item is a modification separately payable after delivery of the device
    and the enlargement or reduction of the device is justified for the claim.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The criteria.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Criterion 1: the condition and its cause.
rule eye_condition with provenance LCD L33737,
        confer "absence or shrinkage of an eye due to birth defect, trauma or surgical removal":
a beneficiary has a qualifying eye condition
    if the beneficiary has a condition of an eye due to a cause
    and the condition is in [absence, shrinkage]
    and the cause is in [birth defect, trauma, surgical removal].

% Criterion 3: the first enlargement or reduction needs no documentation; a
% further one, the record's support — a judgment.
rule eye_first_adjustment with provenance LCD L33737,
        confer "One enlargement (V2625) or reduction (V2626) of the prosthesis is covered without documentation":
the enlargement or reduction of a device is justified for a claim
    if the number of enlargements and reductions of the device previously furnished is a number
    and the number = 0.

rule eye_additional_adjustment with provenance LCD L33737,
        confer "Additional enlargements or reductions are rarely medically necessary and are therefore covered only when there is information in the medical record which supports medical necessity":
the enlargement or reduction of a device is justified for a claim
    if the number of enlargements and reductions of the device previously furnished is a number
    and the number >= 1
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding additional adjustment medically necessary about the beneficiary is established.

% Criterion 4: a modification within 90 days of delivery is in the
% allowance of the prosthesis.
rule eye_modification_timing with provenance Policy Article A52462,
        confer "Modifications to a prosthesis are separately payable when they occur more than 90 days after delivery of the prosthesis":
an item is a modification separately payable after delivery of a device
    if a claim is for the item
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the device was delivered on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number > 90.
